	(text_box "The whole sensing chain lives on this sheet: shunt -> OPA -> ADC, plus terminal sense, supply sense, two position channels and the NTC.\n\n- Rs1 is the ONLY tie between PGND and GND, so all motor return current has to cross it. Don't add another tie in layout. The full layout rules (PGND island, cap returns, Kelvin routing) live in the DRV sheet notes.\n- Lots of DNPs on purpose. This is a swap-and-measure board, populated values are just the starting point.\n- Rk1/Rk2 are 0R walls in front of the amp. If they ever become real resistors, swap BOTH to the same value (thinfilm), or the arms go out of balance.\n- Cc1/Cc2 22pF is the fast config. If it rings, stack the 22pF Cc3/Cc4 pads for a quieter corner.\n- VREF sits at ~0.52V. Stack Rd3 to drop it to ~0.28V.\n- VSNA/VSNB divider bottoms return to VB, not GND, so both terminals stay readable while the bridge coasts and vA - vB is real back-EMF. Rail = 5 x tap - 4 x Vb (divider ratio 0.20); Vb is read at boot with the driver parked, both taps sitting at Vb.\n- POS2 shares its ADC pin with the NTC: JP2 jumped = NTC (internal Rn1/TH1 leg or external J7), JP2 open = second transducer channel. Ra2/Ca2 match Ra1/Ca1 so the pair stays phase-matched.\n- Precision money goes to the shunt + Rg/Rf quad only. Everything else is offset error and boot cal eats it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 209.55 29.21 0)
		(size 72.39 77.2)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.75 1.75)
				(thickness 0.1588)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bfcdfb10-513c-4ea4-8592-ef41fde00e6f")
	)
